      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "97046645-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 1,
      "content": "This agreement displays all lower-division courses required in the major : Stanislaus State courses or requirements on the left, approved (articulated) transfer courses on the right. Helpful resources: Academic Catalog Transfer Admissions Questions regarding this agreement may be directed to the Stanislaus State Articulation Analyst. Please visit the Stanislaus State Articulation Website for contact information.",
      "contentHtml": "<p>This agreement displays all<strong> lower-division courses required in the major</strong>: Stanislaus State courses or requirements on the left, approved (articulated) transfer courses on the right.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Helpful resources: </strong></p><p><a href=\"https://catalog.csustan.edu/index.php\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Academic Catalog</a></p><p><a href=\"https://www.csustan.edu/undergrad/transfer-admission\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Transfer Admissions</a></p><p><br></p><p>Questions regarding this agreement may be directed to the Stanislaus State Articulation Analyst. Please visit the <a href=\"https://www.csustan.edu/articulation\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Stanislaus State Articulation Website</a> for contact information.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "c13d7445-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 2,
      "content": "About the major",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "2eaf7645-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 3,
      "content": "The Anthropology major offers basic preparation for careers requiring contemporary cross-cultural understanding and awareness of cultural heritages. Due to the growing global nature of today’s job market, cross-cultural training is often an employment prerequisite. The major emphasizes archaeology, cultural, biological, medical, visual, and applied aspects of anthropology. It is also designed for students planning to teach social and biological sciences, and for students preparing for graduate work in anthropology and its various geographical areas/interdisciplinary specializations such as such as Latin American Studies, Asian Studies and African Studies. Training in Anthropology is ideal for pursuing a career in many related fields such as forensic science, biology, medicine, public health, law, ux (user experience) research, marketing and market research, public administration, community development, urban planning, and environmental conservation. View information for the Department of Anthropology and Geography/Environmental Resources , including Learning Objectives for the department and its programs.",
      "contentHtml": "<p><span style=\"color: rgb(29, 32, 36);\">The Anthropology major offers basic preparation for careers requiring contemporary cross-cultural understanding and awareness of cultural heritages. Due to the growing global nature of today’s job market, cross-cultural training is often an employment prerequisite. The major emphasizes archaeology, cultural, biological, medical, visual, and applied aspects of anthropology. It is also designed for students planning to teach social and biological sciences, and for students preparing for graduate work in anthropology and its various geographical areas/interdisciplinary specializations such as such as Latin American Studies, Asian Studies and African Studies.&nbsp;Training in Anthropology is ideal for pursuing a career in many related fields such as forensic science, biology, medicine, public health, law, ux (user experience) research, marketing and market research, public administration, community development, urban planning, and environmental conservation.</span></p><p><br></p><p>View information for the <a href=\"https://catalog.csustan.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=35&amp;poid=7797&amp;returnto=6777\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Department of Anthropology and Geography/Environmental Resources</a>, including Learning Objectives for the department and its programs.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "47ef6545-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 4,
      "content": "Note : A wide background in the Social Sciences, Humanities, and Biological Sciences is desirable. Students are encouraged to take introductory courses in related fields within these areas. Students preparing for graduate studies or a research career in anthropology should include a course in statistics, computer science, and at least one language other than English. Students interested in a career in archaeology and/or Cultural Resource Management (CRM) should include a class in Geographic Information Systems (GIS).",
      "contentHtml": "<p><strong style=\"color: rgb(29, 32, 36);\">Note</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(29, 32, 36);\">: A wide background in the Social Sciences, Humanities, and Biological Sciences is desirable. Students are encouraged to take introductory courses in related fields within these areas. Students preparing for graduate studies or a research career in anthropology should include a course in statistics, computer science, and at least one language other than English. Students interested in a career in archaeology and/or Cultural Resource Management (CRM) should include a class in Geographic Information Systems (GIS).</span></p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "35c5955c-deed-4079-897c-0192974f7681",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 5,
      "content": "CONCENTRATIONS IN THE MAJOR",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "d377de59-ff50-4258-b21f-0192974f7681",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 6,
      "content": "Biological Anthropology Interdisciplinary Concentration Please refer to the Anthropology B.A. program page within the Stanislaus State catalog for more details.",
      "contentHtml": "<p><strong>Biological Anthropology Interdisciplinary Concentration</strong></p><p>Please refer to the <a href=\"https://catalog.csustan.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=32&amp;poid=7044&amp;returnto=5379\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Anthropology B.A. program page</a> within the Stanislaus State catalog for more details.</p>"
    }
